# Test: an operator's `request plugin restart <name>` over SSH of a RUNNING
#       external plugin whose process does NOT exit when the daemon stops it
#       still answers, the old process is killed rather than left running
#       beside its replacement, and a new process serves under the name.
# Spec: spec-doctor-coverage-12-plugin-infra R-11
# VALIDATES: ProcessManager.Respawn (internal/component/plugin/process/
#   manager.go) calls proc.Stop(), which cancels the process context and
#   closes its connections, and nothing more: no SIGTERM is sent. On Linux
#   superviseExit (process.go) then waits pluginExitGrace (1s) and SIGKILLs the
#   plugin's process group (pluginGroup.kill, KillProcessGroup) when the plugin
#   has not exited. Respawn joins the old Process for stopExitGrace()+1s (2s),
#   which covers monitorCmd reaping the killed child, then forks the
#   replacement, and restartHandshake (server/restart.go) brings it to
#   StageRunning before handlePluginRestart answers.
# PREVENTS: a restart that hangs on a plugin ignoring its stop, one that leaves
#   the old process running beside its replacement, and one that leaves the
#   name down; and the kill of the old generation reported as a crash or a
#   stop.
# Why not a unit test: the unit tests drive internal plugins, which have no
#   process to outlive their connection. Only a forked plugin that ignores the
#   close reaches superviseExit's kill, and only the daemon route proves the
#   operator's command answers through it.
#
# The harness is test/plugin/plugin-restart-external-running.ci's, which
# carries the reasoning for each piece (no `ze init`, the config user, the
# environment credentials, `ready=Ze running.`). The difference is the
# fixture's argument: plugin/restart-generation ignore-first-stop
# (internal/test/fixture/plugin_fixture_restart_generation.go). Its generation
# 1 records its pid in restart-generation.ignored-stop.pid, ignores SIGTERM and
# SIGINT, and when its connection closes writes
# restart-generation.ignored-stop.held and goes on running for
# restartGenerationHoldMax (60s), so in this test's window only a kill ends
# it. Generation 2 behaves like the sibling's, so the daemon's own stop at the
# end of the test ends it. Bounds on the ignoring process: the daemon's group
# kill in a working product (about 1s after the stop); in a broken one the
# 60s hold, and the plugin's Pdeathsig SIGKILL when the daemon dies.
#
# Budget: the restart costs the 1s exit grace, the reap, a fork and a TLS
# connect-back and handshake. The restart step carries its own 30s bound so a
# hang reads as that step's failure; the await-answer barrier is bounded by
# half the test's budget; the gone check is bounded by 10s. All fit in 60s.

option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ze.ssh.username:value=admin
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass
option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT
tmpfs=running.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
}
plugin {
	external restart-generation {
		run "le test fixture plugin/restart-generation ignore-first-stop"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze start running.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.

# Barrier, state 1: generation 1 runs and serves. Its first answer is where it
# counts itself, records its pid and arms the ignored stop
# (restartGenerationArmIgnore), so the restart below meets a process that will
# not exit on its own.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=le test fixture daemon/await-answer restart-generation-1 "show restart-generation status":exit=0

# The command under test, bounded. Its answer is the handler's Data map:
# message, plugin, was-running (fieldMessage, fieldRestartedPlugin,
# fieldRestartWasRunning, register_plugin_restart.go). It comes only after
# Respawn's join and the replacement's handshake, so an answer at all proves
# the ignored stop did not hang the command.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze cli -c "request plugin restart restart-generation | json":timeout=30s:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=plugin restart-generation was running: stopped and started again
expect=stdout:pattern="was-running":\s*true
expect=stdout:pattern="plugin":\s*"restart-generation"

# A new process serves under the name, with no further barrier: the handler
# answered after restartHandshake reached StageRunning. Generation 1 answering
# would mean the old process still holds the name.
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze cli -c "show restart-generation status":exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=restart-generation-2
reject=stdout:contains=restart-generation-1

# The old process is gone. plugin/restart-generation-gone refuses unless the
# held marker exists, which proves generation 1 ran on past its closed
# connection, so its being gone can only be a kill; it then polls the pid's
# state for at most 10s (no process, or state Z, is gone: daemonProcessState).
# The product prints nothing for the kill (signalLocked logs only a failed
# signal, at debug), so the pid is the observable.
cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=le test fixture plugin/restart-generation-gone:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=ran on past its closed connection and is gone

# The kill of the old generation is the operator's restart, not a crash, and
# leaves no stop record: applyFailurePolicy (server/failure_policy.go) returns
# at its slot check, because Respawn stored the replacement under pm.mu, the
# lock GetProcess takes. The ordering caveat of the sibling test applies: no
# output marks applyFailurePolicy's return, so these rejects are ordered
# against the old generation's RPC loop ending, which the answer waited for.
#
# Nor is it an overlap: the group kill lands 1s after the stop, inside
# Respawn's 2s join (StopJoinBound), so the join completes and
# recordRestartOverlap raises nothing. That raise would come inside Respawn,
# before the restart answered, so this reject is ordered by the answer.
cmd=foreground:seq=6:exec=ze cli -c "show errors | json":exit=0
reject=stdout:contains=doctor-plugin-crashed
reject=stdout:contains=doctor-plugin-restart-overlap
cmd=foreground:seq=7:exec=ze cli -c "show warnings | json":exit=0
reject=stdout:contains=doctor-plugin-stopped
